

 Privacy Policy – Shizuka !!
*Last updated: 10/10/2026

 1. Introduction
- This policy explains what data Shizuka !! collects, how it is used, and how it is protected.
- By using the bot, you agree to this policy.

 2. Data We Collect
- User ID, username and avatar
- Server (guild) ID, name, channel IDs and role IDs
- Commands used and their arguments
- Server settings (prefix, channels, roles, etc.)
- Feature data such as levels/XP, economy balances, warnings, reminders and giveaways
- Moderation records (bans, kicks, mutes, warnings)

 3. Message Tracking
- When enabled, the bot tracks message counts, message IDs, channel IDs and timestamps.
- In some cases, message content is stored for edit/delete logs.
- Used for statistics, leaderboards, moderation and server logs.
- Data is kept only as long as needed for these features.

 4. Invite Tracking
- The bot records which invite a member used to join.
- Stored data includes the inviter's user ID, invite counts and join/leave records.
- Used for invite statistics, leaderboards and inviter rewards.

 5. Ticket System
- The bot stores the ticket ID, channel ID, user ID, category/subject and timestamps.
- Staff members who handled the ticket are also recorded.
- If transcripts are enabled, the full ticket conversation is saved.
- Transcripts may be sent to the server's staff or a log channel.

 6. Welcome System
- The bot stores welcome/leave settings (channel, message, embed, autoroles).
- It uses the new member's username, ID, avatar and join date to send welcome messages and assign roles.
- No extra member data is stored beyond what these features need.

 7. How We Use Data

- To run and provide the bot's features
- For moderation and server security
- To fix bugs and improve performance
- To prevent spam and abuse

 8. Data Sharing
- We do not sell your data.
- We do not share data with third parties, except when required by law or by Discord's official request.

 9. Third-Party Services
- The bot uses the Discord API and hosting/database providers (e.g. [MongoDB / VPS provider]).
- Their own privacy policies apply.

10. Data Storage and Security
- Data is stored in a secured database.
- Only authorized developers can access it.
- No system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.

 11. Data Retention
- Server data is kept while the bot is in the server.
- Data is deleted [30] days after the bot is removed from a server.
- Message logs and ticket transcripts are deleted after [X] days.

 12. Data Deletion
- Users and server owners can request data deletion via [email / support server].
- Requests are processed within [7] days.

 13. User Rights
- You can request access to your data.
- You can request correction of your data.
- You can request deletion of your data.

 14. Changes to This Policy
- We may update this policy from time to time.
- Major changes will be announced in the support server.

